WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
- We're back and this
hour we're unlocking our

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.780
vault to share never
before seen stories from

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.430
some of our favorite guests.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:09.480
We always love having
Melissa McCarthy here

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.190
mostly because also I see her at home.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.350
She's my neighbor, but
she's cool here too.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.270
Um, on a recent visit, she shared a letter

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.610
she had written to herself years ago,

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:21.400
basically words of wisdom
she wanted to embrace.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.440
So it included things like in 10 years,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.470
you won't remember his name and

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.320
just eat the damn cookie.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.550
So here's some more of
what Melissa had to say.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:31.427
And then there is

00:00:31.427 --> 00:00:34.047
"A walk of shame can
be character building".

00:00:34.966 --> 00:00:36.655
(applause and cheer)

00:00:36.655 --> 00:00:38.052
- Right!

00:00:38.052 --> 00:00:40.169
- So, we've all had them

00:00:40.169 --> 00:00:42.660
- We've all had them guys,
if you haven't, I suggest it.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.540
- Most of them may have been in Vegas.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.530
(laughter)

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.800
So which walk was most
character building for you?

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.060
- I will say. Sorry, mom and dad.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.530
That was in college. I was walking home.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.180
I was very Gothic in college,

00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:00.510
so it's like huge blue
black hair, full length cape

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.170
stacked crazy like,

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.720
combat boots or like
seventies go-go boots.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.290
No one was dressing like this at the time.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.500
And it was the next morning.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.390
And I was walking along on campus,

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:11.780
like kind of on a highway.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.140
And I thought, this is not my best moment

00:01:16.096 --> 00:01:18.430
because there was no way I was like,

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.090
I'm up and getting coffee.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.210
I had like glitter,

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:24.240
and it was very much an evening look.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.450
And an evening look
for someone who is very

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.660
like punk rock.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.520
So at like eight in the
morning, I was like, ah, right.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.390
But then I thought, you know,
I look back on that now,

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:35.597
And I'm like, eh, who cares?

00:01:35.597 --> 00:01:37.200
- But I like the
character building though.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.450
- It is because I'm like that,

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.010
whatever that experience
was, I was like, it's,

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:44.700
again it's all the, it's
laying the foundation.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.770
And I'm like, oh, well.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:47.720
- I love that. I love.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:50.890
Okay. So you also wrote go all in.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:53.480
You'll never get today back. I love this.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.210
So before your career started,

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:56.800
you were almost going to quit, right?

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:57.647
I did not know this.

00:01:57.647 --> 00:01:58.480
- Yeah

00:01:58.480 --> 00:01:59.520
I think. It was like, I-

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.280
- I almost quit at the beginning of mine.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.680
- Did you really? God that
would have been terrible.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.350
- Like right after idol.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.850
- After idol you almost
did? Are you kidding?

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:09.300
- No, I literally called
my mom and I was like,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.790
on the way to, I was like,
this is not my people,

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.640
these aren't my people.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.850
I was like, yeah.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:16.430
- You know you get
something you still have to

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.340
navigate are these the right crowd

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.000
- Yeah and like, who's around you,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.230
You have no control when you're
19 or 20. And I was like,

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.950
this is not like, look here,

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.220
I was a good waitress,

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.310
- I liked waiting tables.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.220
- I liked waiting tables. I love people

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.210
- I can hem pants, I can sew.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:32.450
- Yeah I'm like, I can quilt.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:33.636
See we have so much in common?

00:02:33.636 --> 00:02:36.600
No, I'm just saying I've been
at that point too though.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.040
When it's like, it's
like, oh, I'm just, uh

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.960
it's not, what's worth it.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.343
- What's worth it. And to,

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:46.130
and the thing of trying
not to live with regrets,

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.730
you know, or being
like, oh, I should have,

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.000
it's like the car ride home.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.440
Like I wish I would have said, you know,

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.100
without going crazy. But like,

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.447
I don't like how you talk
to me or I don't like,

00:02:55.447 --> 00:02:57.689
how this is happening or
can we do it differently?

00:02:57.689 --> 00:03:00.890
Blah, blah, blah. I did
so many on the way home

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:04.350
It is always like, God,
am I good in the car.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.660
Cause on the way home, it is like

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.640
I would always like figure it out.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.022
- Like download everything that, yeah.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:13.230
- But the bells, the red flag
was going off in the moment.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.450
I just didn't listen to it.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:19.450
And I think we have this
incredibly loud bell, big red flag.

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:22.290
And we haven't because when

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.340
something's not right, we know it.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:25.970
And then we're kind of taught to, I think,

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.372
especially as women, but I think everybody

00:03:27.372 --> 00:03:31.190
we tend to, we're kind
of taught and trained

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:32.410
to be like don't make fast.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:33.243
- Don't ruffle feathers.

00:03:33.243 --> 00:03:34.210
- Don't be crazy.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.600
Like just let it go, blah, blah, blah.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.930
And it's like, we don't
have to like, you know,

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.420
I'm not pulling out switchblades,

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:42.264
but I try to like complete
each day. And in the

00:03:42.264 --> 00:03:44.460
moment, be like, wait a minute.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.390
Let's, this is going, this is going in a

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.674
direction that's maybe
not great for anybody.

00:03:48.674 --> 00:03:50.700
And it's always better to talk about

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.410
it in the moment than
regret it the next day,

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.030
cause you can't go back.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.460
You can't go back to that moment

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.420
and take care of it and
take care of yourself

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.450
in the moment. So I try to be,

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:01.549
I guess it's part of being present.

00:04:01.549 --> 00:04:02.798
- Yeah, no one hurt,
and that's hard to do.

00:04:02.798 --> 00:04:04.390
- It's a process.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.970
- And it's also sticking up for yourself.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.150
I think that was what ended up.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:08.490
My mom was like the

00:04:09.494 --> 00:04:12.570
super nurturing moment for her. But she,

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:15.200
she was, she said to me, she was like,

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.570
don't let, you're not you don't,

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:19.220
you're not liking it because
of what you said originally.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.180
Like, I don't like how
people are talking to me.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:22.950
I don't like how they're talking
about me. Like I'm product.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.050
Like I don't want to do this.

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:26.640
I don't want to be naked on the
cover. I don't want to like,

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.310
it's just not me. It's like, if it was me,

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.190
I'd totally do it. But it
was one of those things

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.700
where she was like, don't
let somebody else like

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.330
steal your moment because
they don't like how

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.888
you want to do it. Like it's you that-

00:04:34.888 --> 00:04:37.290
So anyway, it was just
kind of like good words,

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.650
like fight for yourself in those moments.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.496
- It is, and it's like, you can fight,

00:04:40.496 --> 00:04:44.140
you can fight for yourself,
still with kindness.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.530
You don't have to be like combative.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:48.000
Sometimes maybe you have to be, but it is-

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.940
- I hated that when I was young, did you?

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.312
I hated confrontation.

00:04:51.312 --> 00:04:52.180
- That's why I stopped.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:55.790
I started in standup and it's
why I stopped because there's

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:57.410
always, by the way, there's always a guy

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:59.870
in every club going "take your top off."

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:03.142
And you're like, when has
that ever worked for you?

00:05:03.142 --> 00:05:04.684
Like when is yelling,

00:05:04.684 --> 00:05:06.590
and a women be like, oh
my God, you're right.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:09.290
You know, it's like, I
just thought, and the

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.610
only way you could get them to stop,

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.010
you had to shame them until they were

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.074
so embarrassed that they stopped talking.

00:05:16.074 --> 00:05:17.030
- Yeah.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:19.650
- And I would finish up
my little set and then

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:21.470
I would feel terrible because I was like,

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:24.150
I just wanted to tell some weird story

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:27.600
about my day, And I
ended up making this guy,

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:28.870
that's yelling, take your top off,

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.984
which means he's probably not doing great,

00:05:30.984 --> 00:05:32.817
and I had to make him feel really,

00:05:32.817 --> 00:05:35.020
really bad about himself in order

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.160
to make him stop talking.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.850
And he shouldn't have been
yelling take your top off.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.340
- Also though maybe
you're the one person that

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:40.850
finally told him to shut up, so.

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:45.097
- Maybe, and I did not. Mom,
I did not take my top off.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.330
So that's, that's one for me.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.210
- I have to show this video because

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:52.420
I have not seen this movie ever.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.253
- Oh god, yes.

00:05:53.253 --> 00:05:54.799
- So I have to show this tape.

00:05:54.799 --> 00:05:57.051
- It was going to be a
boxing movie, it wasn't.

00:05:57.051 --> 00:05:59.353
(laughing and crying)

00:05:59.353 --> 00:06:01.630
(melancholic piano sounds)

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:02.840
- It was really beautiful.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.413
Oh my god she was, perfect.

00:06:05.413 --> 00:06:07.013
Oh my God. It's so difficult.

00:06:07.901 --> 00:06:10.560
(more laughter and crying)

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.990
(cheers and applause)

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.190
- Oh my god, it's so difficult.

00:06:16.963 --> 00:06:20.040
- There's always- By the way that's

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.360
my niceness in Sammy
that as I was sobbing,

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.363
she's like, let me get the camera.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.600
But I had not. You lose some,
just sometimes those movies

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.610
that you're like, there is
no reason I didn't see it.

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:33.490
You just miss it. I don't read reviews.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:35.530
I don't like to know what a
movie is going to be about.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:37.570
I like to be surprised.
And so it was like,

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.540
oh my God, how did I not see this movie?

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.110
I do this movie club on zoom.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.970
So I was like, this week
it's million dollar baby.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.930
I'm like, I don't know much
about boxing, but I'm being,

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:49.190
maybe it's a fish out of water
or something like friends

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:51.540
that, you know, unlikely
friends and we're watching it.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.520
And I'm like, oh, this is nice.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:56.020
And the two people I was
watching with kept going,

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.890
they kept looking at me and I
was like, what are you doing?

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:02.050
They're like, you don't
know what this is about.

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:04.236
I'm like, it's about boxing.

00:07:04.236 --> 00:07:05.069
- That's what I think.

00:07:05.069 --> 00:07:06.210
And then it hit a certain,

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.560
there's a certain moment in it.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.900
That is so devastating.
And you have no idea.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:11.970
Who's seen the movie.

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:12.870
- I've not seen it.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:16.550
It is a spectacular, it's so good.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:17.550
- I don't want to cry.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:18.383
- and it's something

00:07:18.383 --> 00:07:21.220
you want to see once
because Hillary Swank is,

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:23.440
is perfection in it.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.920
but I was crying so hard and
I could not get it together.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.550
And I like wept for like 20 minutes.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.383
And everybody who-

00:07:29.383 --> 00:07:31.390
- Do you love that? I love that release

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:33.050
- The next day I was like, I'm good.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.350
I'm good for like a month.

